.TH PSVectorFill 3 2023-12-07 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSVectorFill

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
void  
.br
\fBPSVectorFill\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIPSFloat val\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fill vector \fIvec\fR having length defined by \fIlen\fR with \fIvalue\fR. The function will immediately return if \fIvec\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIlen\fR is zero.
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.
